  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_forward_pass(X: list, W1: list, b1: list, W2: list, b2: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Multi-Layer Perceptron (Forward Pass)** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_forward_pass(X: list, W1: list, b1: list, W2: list, b2: list) -> list:\n    h = np.maximum(0.0, np.array(X, dtype=float) @ np.array(W1, dtype=float) + np.array(b1, dtype=float))\n    return np.round(h @ np.array(W2, dtype=float) + np.array(b2, dtype=float), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
